---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout id="pipeline" title="Pipeline">

  <h1>Pipeline</h1>

  <h2>Temp</h2>

  <p>
    Unused issue slots can be filled with NOPs. The important point for the pipeline is that the
    molecule already describes a statically scheduled group of native operations; the hardware
    does not dynamically perform a conventional out-of-order scheduling step.
  </p>


  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Operation</th><th>Pipeline</th><th>What to remember</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Integer / ALU</td>
          <td><code>Fetch0 → Fetch1 → Decode → Register → Execute → Write → Commit</code></td>
          <td>Short integer execution path with commit at the end.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Load / Store</td>
          <td><code>Fetch0 → Fetch1 → Register → Mem0 → Mem1 → Write → Commit</code></td>
          <td>Memory stages initiate/complete the cache access and associated checks.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Floating point</td>
          <td><code>Fetch0 → Fetch1 → Register → A → B → C → D → Write → Commit</code></td>
          <td>Longer pipeline than simple integer execution.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Branch</td>
          <td><code>Predict → Wait → Wait → Wait → Verify</code></td>
          <td>Follow a predicted path while the branch resolves, then verify it.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>


</Layout>
